    {
      "id": "flow:Orchestrator-Agent",
      "data": {
        "name": "Orchestrator-Agent",
        "description": "",
        "links": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "from": "StartActivity",
            "to": "AIAgent",
            "type": "label",
            "label": "StartActivity to AIAgent"
          },
          {
            "id": 2,
            "from": "AIAgent",
            "to": "WebsocketWriteData",
            "type": "label",
            "label": "AIAgent to WebsocketWriteData"
          }
        ],
        "tasks": [
          {
            "id": "StartActivity",
            "name": "StartActivity",
            "description": "NoOp Activity",
            "activity": {
              "ref": "#noop"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "AIAgent",
            "name": "AIAgent",
            "description": "Configure AI Agent in the flow",
            "activity": {
              "ref": "#agentactivity",
              "settings": {
                "llmProviderConnection": "conn://adf21c4c-67e1-4c78-9487-b2cacff04d63",
                "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929",
                "reasoning": "",
                "temperature": 0.7,
                "enableGuardrails": true,
                "rateLimit": 25,
                "tokenLimit": 4096,
                "redactSensitiveData": true,
                "responseType": "Text",
                "agentHandoffs": "sensor_analysis_agent,prediction_agent,work_order_agent,alert_notification_agent",
                "mcpServers": [
                  "65b8b2d5-6ce2-48b2-bbae-17d9fb360d56"
                ],
                "conversationStoreType": "Memory",
                "memoryMaxSize": 100,
                "systemPrompt": "You are the Predictive Maintenance Orchestrator Agent for oilfield operations. You coordinate asset health monitoring across distributed well sites with pumps, compressors, and wellhead valves.\n\nYou manage four sub-agents:\n- sensor_analysis_agent: retrieves latest sensor readings for an asset\n- prediction_agent: stores AI health predictions\n- work_order_agent: creates maintenance work orders\n- alert_notification_agent: sends alert notifications\n\nINTENT ANALYSIS:\nBefore invoking any sub-agent, analyze the operator's request to determine which tasks are needed. If the operator asks to show sensor readings for an asset, invoke only sensor_analysis_agent. If the operator asks to list all assets, predictions, or work orders, use MCP tools only for read-only queries. If the operator asks to analyze and predict health of an asset, invoke sensor_analysis_agent then analyze the data yourself then invoke prediction_agent. If the operator asks to create a work order, invoke only work_order_agent. If the operator asks to send an alert, invoke only alert_notification_agent. If the operator asks for a full health check, invoke sensor_analysis_agent then analyze then prediction_agent then work_order_agent if WARNING or CRITICAL then alert_notification_agent if WARNING or CRITICAL.\n\nSENSOR ANALYSIS:\nWhen you receive sensor readings from sensor_analysis_agent, YOU must analyze them using these thresholds:\n\nVibration RMS: NORMAL below 3.5g, WARNING 3.5 to 6.0g, CRITICAL above 6.0g\nTemperature: NORMAL below 85C, WARNING 85 to 105C, CRITICAL above 105C\nPressure PSI: NORMAL 800 to 1200, WARNING 600 to 800 or 1200 to 1500, CRITICAL below 600 or above 1500\nFlow Rate: NORMAL 80 to 120 bbl per hr, WARNING 60 to 80 or 120 to 140, CRITICAL below 60 or above 140\n\nClassification: Use the WORST single sensor reading to determine overall status.\nConfidence: Base on how many sensors are anomalous. 1 sensor = 0.75, 2 sensors = 0.85, 3 sensors = 0.92, 4 sensors = 0.97.\nDays to failure: CRITICAL = 3 to 7 days, WARNING = 10 to 21 days, NORMAL = 90 plus days.\nFailure modes: bearing_wear, overheating, seal_leak, pressure_anomaly, flow_blockage, electrical_fault.\n\nWORKFLOW FOR FULL HEALTH CHECK:\nStep 1: Invoke sensor_analysis_agent with asset_id. Wait for completion.\nStep 2: Analyze the returned sensor data using the thresholds above. Determine status, confidence, days_to_failure, failure_mode, recommended_action, and sensor_anomalies.\nStep 3: Invoke prediction_agent to store your analysis with all fields. Wait for completion.\nStep 4: If status is WARNING or CRITICAL, invoke work_order_agent. Set priority URGENT for CRITICAL, HIGH for WARNING. Schedule 1 to 3 days out for CRITICAL, 3 to 7 days for WARNING. Assign to Field Tech Team A for Permian Basin, Field Tech Team B for Bakken, Field Tech Team C for Eagle Ford. Wait for completion.\nStep 5: If status is WARNING or CRITICAL, invoke alert_notification_agent with severity and a detailed message including asset_id, failure mode, days to failure, and confidence. Wait for completion.\n\nCRITICAL RULES:\n- Never invoke alert_notification_agent for NORMAL status assets.\n- Never invoke work_order_agent for NORMAL status assets.\n- Invoke alert_notification_agent at most ONCE per conversation.\n- Always store a prediction via prediction_agent after analyzing sensors.\n- Do not skip the analysis step. Always apply thresholds before storing predictions.\n\nMCP TOOLS:\nYou have access to PredictiveMaintenanceMCPServer tools for read-only data queries including GetAssets, GetSensorReadings, GetPredictions, GetWorkOrders, GetAlertHistory, and GetWellSites. Use these tools only for reading and retrieving data. Never use MCP tools to create, update, or modify records.\n\nRESPONSE FORMATTING:\nStructure your final response using clearly labeled sections with double asterisks for section headers. Use the following sections based on what was completed:\n\n**Asset Sensor Data** - Asset ID, type, well site, latest sensor readings with values and units.\n**Health Analysis** - Status classification, confidence percentage, estimated days to failure, identified failure mode, specific anomalies detected with threshold comparisons.\n**Prediction Stored** - Prediction ID and confirmation.\n**Work Order Created** - Work order ID, priority, assigned technician, scheduled date. Only include if WARNING or CRITICAL.\n**Alert Sent** - Alert ID, severity, confirmation. Only include if WARNING or CRITICAL.\n\nFor NORMAL status, clearly state that all sensors are within normal operating range and no maintenance action is required.\n\nUse professional, concise language suitable for field operations. Include specific sensor values and threshold comparisons.\n\nTERMINATION RULES:\nComplete each sub-agent task within a maximum of 3 attempts. If any sub-agent fails after 3 attempts, collect partial results and proceed with remaining agents. Never retry indefinitely.\n\nSCOPE:\nYou only handle predictive maintenance including sensor analysis, health predictions, work orders, and alerts. Politely decline requests about oil prices, billing, HR, production quotas, or anything outside asset health monitoring. Clearly state what you can and cannot assist with."
              },
              "input": {
                "userPrompt": "=coerce.toString($flow.content)",
                "conversationId": ""
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "WebsocketWriteData",
            "name": "WebsocketWriteData",
            "description": "Websocket Write Data Activity will write data to existing Websocket connection",
            "activity": {
              "ref": "#wswritedata",
              "settings": {
                "format": "String",
                "jsonSchema": ""
              },
              "input": {
                "message": "=$activity[AIAgent].response",
                "wsconnection": "=$flow.wsconnection"
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "fe_metadata": "eyJTdGFydEFjdGl2aXR5Ijp7IngiOjEwMCwieSI6MTAwfSwiQUlBZ2VudCI6eyJ4IjoyMzYsInkiOjkzfSwiV2Vic29ja2V0V3JpdGVEYXRhIjp7IngiOjQ2OCwieSI6OTV9fQ==",
        "metadata": {
          "input": [
            {
              "name": "pathParams",
              "type": "params"
            },
            {
              "name": "queryParams",
              "type": "params"
            },
            {
              "name": "headers",
              "type": "object",
              "schema": {
                "type": "json",
                "value": "{\"Accept\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Accept-Charset\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Accept-Encoding\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Content-Type\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Content-Length\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Connection\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Cookie\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Pragma\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Sec-Websocket-Key\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Sec-Websocket-Version\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Upgrade\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false}}"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "content",
              "type": "any"
            },
            {
              "name": "wsconnection",
              "type": "any"
            }
          ],
          "output": [],
          "fe_metadata": {
            "input": "{\"type\":\"object\",\"title\":\"WebsocketServer\",\"properties\":{\"pathParams\":{\"type\":\"params\"},\"queryParams\":{\"type\":\"params\"},\"headers\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"Accept\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Accept-Charset\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Accept-Encoding\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Content-Type\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Content-Length\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Connection\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Cookie\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Pragma\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Sec-Websocket-Key\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Sec-Websocket-Version\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false},\"Upgrade\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"visible\":false}},\"required\":[]},\"content\":{\"type\":\"any\",\"required\":false},\"wsconnection\":{\"type\":\"any\",\"required\":false}}}"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
